      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JOSEPHINE'S BOY (2) is the top pick after a solid local run last start, placing well and showing he can handle this track. Though he was beaten by New Prospect, this maiden isn't particularly tough, and his overall record here and at this distance makes him the one to beat. HYDRATING (5) is a key threat after finishing second at Eidsvold behind Moonspell and a luckless fourth here, where she was held up and only missed by under two lengths. However, her winless record at 1170m is a concern, though her recent form keeps her competitive. LUSTFUL BELLE (6) comes off a strong run, finishing second at Talwood despite a tough trip. With an apprentice claim, she poses a serious winning threat if she can replicate that effort. FLYING ZULU (13) hasn't placed in six starts but showed promise with a decent fifth at Warwick despite covering ground; a return to this trip might see him in the placings.",
